# Dealtitude — hosting rules.
#
# One rule, on purpose. Every path serves the app, and the app asks the server
# which shop the path names. So a new shop's counter card works the moment the
# shop exists in the database — no rewrite rule to add here, no redeploy, and
# no chance of a printed card pointing at a line somebody forgot to write.
#
# The 200 matters: it serves index.html at the URL the visitor typed, so the
# path is still readable by the app. A 301 or 302 would throw the shop name
# away before the app ever saw it, and every printed card would land on the
# ZIP screen.

# These two come FIRST, because the catch-all below would otherwise swallow
# them and serve the app instead. Apple requires a working privacy policy URL
# and a working support URL, and both are checked by a person.
/privacy    /privacy.html   200
/support    /support.html   200

/*    /index.html   200
